; A stand-in for the owner's session (CART.9, decision 14; its first slice), written by the engine's own steps in the
; form the host's recorder writes, so that the page's hand of the bench, the block hand-naught, holds a replay. The
; load's act, the selection at A1 on the Bench; then thirty-eight switches written one an act, each a row of the
; drawer's edit row. The adder's a set to all ones, a bit an act, then its carry-in: the deepest ripple, 65,535 + 1
; carried through all sixteen bits to 65,536. The multiplier's a set to 1 and its b to all ones, 1 x 255, then the
; rest of its a, 255 x 255 = 65,025. Then the adder's b low bit on, 65,537, and its a low bit off, 65,536; the
; multiplier's a low bit off, 254 x 255 = 64,770, and its b high bit off, 254 x 127 = 32,258; and the carry-in off,
; 65,534 + 1 = 65,535. The bench settles: each act is its own frame and one that proves nothing moved, a settle's
; frame holding no row, so 39 acts are 78 frames, every gate held to the hand at each. Its golden is the Bench's
; record at its end.
; The owner's session replaces it at the hand test.
